A recorded `kdos-power firewall list`.

The surface carries no table of services — kdos-powerd owns it, because a
client that could name a port could open any port. That makes the picture
depend on a running daemon, which a golden may not, so KDOS_FIREWALL_LIST
points here instead.

Two services are `on` on purpose: a golden of a machine with nothing open
would not show what an open row looks like, and "open" is drawn in the warning
slot rather than the accent precisely because it is the state worth noticing.
